course: dictionary
lesson: 769
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The word bear can mean an animal, a soft toy, or to carry a weight. The sentence around it tells you which meaning is right. «Bears come to food smells at a campsite, so people store food safely.» Here bears are big, wild animals, because they come to food and people must lock it away.
explain: Look for clues in the words near bear. If the sentence talks about weight, carrying or holding up, bear is a verb meaning to carry. «The bridge can bear 10 tons» means the bridge can hold up 10 tons.
explain: If the sentence talks about feelings or noise, bear may mean to put up with something. «I cannot bear the noise» means I cannot put up with the noise. Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the word.
fact: Bear can be a noun (an animal, or a teddy bear) or a verb (to carry, or to put up with).
fact: A polar bear lives in the Arctic, and bears can hibernate, which means they sleep through the winter.
fact: «Bears come to food smells at a campsite.» So in parks with bears, you keep food locked away and never go near a bear.
fact: To bear means to carry or hold up a weight: the bridge can bear 10 tons.
fact: To bear fruit means to grow fruit, and bear in mind means to remember something.
exercise: «Bears come to food smells at a campsite.» What are bears in this sentence? | To carry something heavy | *Big, strong animals with thick fur | Soft toys | To put up with something
exercise: «The bridge can bear 10 tons.» What does bear mean here? | To grow fruit | *To carry or hold up a weight | To put up with noise | To sleep through the winter
exercise: «I cannot bear the noise.» Which meaning fits? | A big animal with thick fur | A soft toy | To hold up a weight | *To put up with it
test: Which phrase names a soft toy? | bear in mind | polar bear | *teddy bear | bear fruit
test: Which meaning of bear is right in «The trees bear fruit in autumn»? | to put up with | a big animal | *to grow fruit | to carry a weight
exam: Which sentence uses bear to mean to carry a weight? | *The bridge can bear 10 tons, so trucks may cross it | A polar bear lives in the Arctic | The bridge can bear 10 tons | I cannot bear the noise
